    "body": "Thanks @annevk. I'll try better in the next PRs but please bear with me if I'm doing a wrong wrapping again. ;) Not sure if I understood your rule here. Especially:\n\n```\n       attribute whose value is not the empty string, then <span data-x=\"resolve a\n       url\">resolve</span> the value of that attribute to an <span>absolute URL</span>, relative to\n```\n\nCouldn't it wrap after `url\">` or even `url\">resolve`? If there's any pointer to refer to or brief description will help. But never mind if you don't have any existing reference. Don't want it to bother you.\n\nAnd you call other specs \"specification\" e.g. File API specification. So out of curiosity, what's the difference there?\n",
